Subject: Add explicit CPU PQ3 cache graphs with signed-Hadamard transforms and fail-closed state policy
Base: llama.cpp a34de8618b25dfc32ee43749db47d767a9f0a25d (b12015), after 0003-0008
License: MIT; pinned upstream LICENSE and earlier PQ3 donor attribution retained

Why: type traits alone do not define cache graph transforms or persistence.
Graph ABI v1 composes D then plain normalized H128 for Q/K/V, H128 then D
on attention output. Fixed masks and bit order are tested; only plain H receives
the GGML Hadamard hint. Ordinary and hybrid full/SWA graphs use the same policy.
Explicit CPU-only, causal, single-sequence Llama/LFM3 PQ3/PQ3 contexts are allowed;
other policies fail before allocation. No GPU scheduler fallback is advertised.
Prototype state I/O and positional shifts fail before IO or hybrid mutation.
No context-parameter or PQ3 row-layout change. Internal memory vtables gain a
codec capability; all native consumers/shims must use the composed headers.
Separate graph ABI symbols prevent confusing row-only builds with live graphs.
Tests: test-pq3-graph plus CPU model smoke/lifecycle and guarded binding tests.

